<title>USA: St Joseph hogs up $1.00 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs up $1.00 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with Thursday, barrows and gilts were $1.00 higher. Top $54.00 per cwt.</p>
<p>Much improved weather conditions early in the week and hogs moved, prices dropped. Receipts dried up and with liberal early week slaughter, packers crying for kill numbers from mid-week on. Majority of tight supplies locked up in big hog factories.</p>
<p>    US 1-3    230-270 lbs    53.50-54.00</p>
<p>    US 2-3    270-290 lbs    52.00-53.00</p>
<p>    Sows - up $0.50-2.00. Top $52.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-2    300-500 lbs    43.50</p>
<p>    US 1-3    500-550 lbs    49.00</p>
<p>		  550-700 lbs    51.00-52.00</p>
</text>
